96,southwest,"You will notice that the wall blocking the path to the south is repeated 3 times. Therefore, it seems that this wall is actually a continuous vertical wall, separating the north part of the room from the south part of the room. To move south, the wall must be traversed. From the description of the room and the observation, the open door in the west direction is in the north part of the room. The stair up is in the west direction, but it is not possible to go up because there is no available door that leads to the stairs up. Our ultimate goal is to find the stair down. The stair up seems to be related to the stair down. Therefore, we need to traverse the room to reach the stair up first. As the west wall is an open door and the stair up is near west, we can move to the stair up after opening the stair up door. This stair up will lead us to the next level. To move south, we need to go north first to find a passage or open door that leads us to the south part of the room. Therefore, our plan is to search for an open door that can lead us to the south part of the room, move through the open door, then move to the stair up and finally find the stair down.","message:
